In article <12395@mentor.cc.purdue.edu> ach@mentor.cc.purdue.edu (Joseph Poirier) writes:
>   I have recently been playing 'hack' on a Sparc (hack version 1.0.2).  I
>have figured several things out, but the problem I (and others here) keep
>having is the dreaded cockatrice.  If you don't kill it within two turns,
>it almost always hisses and turns you to stone.  
>   Is there a sure-fire way to get around this?  We have tried 'wielding'
>a dead lizard (is that what dead lizards are used for?), but that didn't
>do anything when I hit the cockatrice with it.  Should I have thrown it
>instead, or am I on the wrong track?  I can't seem to find a mirror.  Is
>there a way I can avert my gaze?  

The dead lizard doesn't help you by wielding it; it helps you in that it reduces
the otherwise excessively-high chance of being turned to stone on a new moon
night to normal.  To get this effect, just carry it.  (The fortune cookie
message saying to wield it is bogus.)

1.0.3 allowed you to eat a dead acid blob _after_ the hiss got you, to prevent
being turned to stone.  I don't remember if 1.0.2 allowed this.  (If 1.0.2
causes hissing to _immediately_ turn you to stone, instead of after a few
moves, then this won't work.)

Mirrors do not exist in Hack, and in Nethack they don't work against
cockatrices.

Also, if you're having trouble, you might want to consider engraving
'Elbereth' on the ground with your fingers, then throwing stuff at the
cockatrice (or other monster).  (This doesn't work in 1.0.3 or in Nethack.)
